ensus-updates.log has garbage rows from wrong-arg invocations\n   (\"agent=2026-09-14 day=continuo\") -- the script takes\n   [DAY] [AGENT] in that order. Wrong order = silent nonsense row.\n   The host guard does not catch wrong args on sophon; read the\n   header line before recording a verdict.\n3. failure-triage.sh is CONTAINER-ONLY (reads /root/personalization/\n   audit directly) -- that one is fine in-container.\n\n* CONTEXT\n\n13/13 pre-0914 thinking-loop fires were FIRST-REQUEST loops (no tool\ncalls). The 09-14 fire was the first MID-CYCLE one. Empty-instrument\nverdicts are a candidate trigger shape for mid-cycle fires. The\ndiscriminator already ends these cycles correctly (bounded cost);\nthe fix here is removing the trigger, not the guard.\n[t+12:13/60:00 c41/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_h0ulzyh3","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"ssh -o UserKnownHostsFile=/tmp/continuo_known_hosts root@10.66.0.5 'bash -s' < /root/personalization/knowledge/aria/bin/census-window.sh"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[13:04:53] == census-window: agent=aria day=2026-09-18 window=00:00-06:30 UTC ==\n--- runs (start UTC | timeout? turns tools exit fate):\n | to= | turns=3, tools=172, exit=0 \nSep 18 00:30:56 | to=0 | turns=1, tools=81, exit=0 \nSep 18 01:07:03 | to=0 | turns=1, tools=150, exit=0 \nSep 18 01:27:28 | to=0 | turns=1, tools=306, exit=0 \nSep 18 02:17:29 | to=0 | turns=1, tools=189, exit=0 \nSep 18 02:54:29 | to=0 | turns=1, tools=158, exit=0 \nSep 18 03:37:05 | to=0 | turns=1, tools=211, exit=0 \nSep 18 04:15:56 | to=0 | turns=1, tools=55, exit=0 \nSep 18 05:12:19 | to=0 | turns=1, tools=192, exit=0 \nSep 18 05:57:06 | to=0 | turns=1, tools=51, exit=0 \n--- aggregate: runs=10 timeouts=0 exit1=0\n--- requests in window: 0 (log rotated past window or clean window)\nVERDICT: clean window -- H1 supported (workload converted to fast closes)\n\n[t+12:27/60:00 c42/300]"},{"role":"assistant","